PS5 Bluetooth: Pro, MediaTek and IW620 fixes, and the USB controller they sit on

- Pro (0e8d:3605; QuartConz, mfoster978 PR #30): HCI on interface 3 with the IF3 routing undone before setup
  and shutdown (setup re-runs at every power on), the first HCI Reset retried after a cold boot, ACL on bulk
  OUT 0x0d, no autosuspend. Replaces the early draft in rmux's tree.
- MediaTek (0e8d:3603): no ISO interface setup (ps5-linux-patches #71). It times out, and the reset after it
  leaves Bluetooth broken after a warm restart until a cold boot.
- IW620 (1286:2059; ps5-linux-patches #75): the repeated Just Works link key request right after pairing gets
  the key the controller just reported (ps5_iw620_linkkey=0 turns it off); LL privacy and the extended LE
  features are hidden from the stack (ps5_iw620_le=0 turns it off).
- Salina xHCI (ps5-linux-patches #78, Slip): it doesn't return from runtime D3, and the Bluetooth chip on it
  was lost until a cold start; a runtime PM reference keeps it in D0 even when userspace sets power/control
  to auto.
